{{ .ProjectName }} is a Go CLI project generated by `go-cli-starter`.

## Quick Start

```bash
go mod tidy
go build -o bin/{{ .BinaryName }} ./main.go
./bin/{{ .BinaryName }} version
```

## Commands

- `version`: print build and version info
{{- if not .Minimal }}
- `greet --name World`: sample command for Cobra usage
- `mcp`: start MCP server with a sample `hello` tool (`stdio`/`sse`/`http`)

## MCP Layering

- `cmd/mcp.go`: thin CLI entry, delegates to internal package
- `internal/mcp/server.go`: builds server, transport wrappers, config loading
- `internal/mcp/handler/*`: tool registration + request parsing
- `internal/mcp/service/*`: business logic called by handlers

## MCP Usage

```bash
# stdio (default)
./bin/{{ .BinaryName }} mcp

# sse
./bin/{{ .BinaryName }} mcp --transport sse --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8080

# http
./bin/{{ .BinaryName }} mcp --transport http --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8080

# all transports
./bin/{{ .BinaryName }} mcp --transport all --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8080
# all mode: SSE listens on 8080, HTTP listens on 8081

# load from config
./bin/{{ .BinaryName }} mcp --config docs/examples/mcp.json
# note: enable_stdio/enable_sse/enable_http are used when transport=all
```
{{- end }}

## Included Utilities

- `pkg/log`: zap logger wrapper with stdio/stderr/file output
- `utils/time_util`: shared timestamp layout constants
- `utils/retry`: retry helpers with exponential backoff + jitter
- `utils/http_util`: HTTP client wrapper with retry and JSON helpers
- `utils/file_util`: common file helpers (exists/copy/json read-write)

